 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "addSong(title) stores a song and returns its id; ids are 1, 2, 3, ... in call order and never reused; titles may repeat. playSong(songId, userId) records that the user played the song (void). getAnalytics() returns [title, number of DISTINCT users who played the song] for every song, sorted by that count descending, ties by smaller song id (output form and tie rule inferred). Level 2 adds getLastThreeSongs(userId): the ids of the (up to) three most recently played DISTINCT songs of that user, most recent first; an unknown user gets [] (method name and id output inferred). Level 3 adds removeSong(songId): true and removes the song if it exists and is not removed yet, else false. Removed songs disappear from getAnalytics and getLastThreeSongs (older songs move up), later plays of them are ignored, and ids are not reused.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk03-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
